# Avendavi runtime env.
#
# IMPORTANT: anything prefixed `VITE_` is inlined at *build time* by Vite,
# not read at runtime. For Docker, pass these as `--build-arg` in the build
# step (or expose them via `args:` in docker-compose.yml) and reference them
# via `ARG VITE_FOO` in the Dockerfile. They are NOT picked up from this
# file by the running container.
#
# The admin login from an earlier version was removed during the rebrand
# to Avendavi. The placeholder below is kept so it can be flipped back on
# later without re-discovering the variable name.

# Admin passphrase SHA-256 hash. Generate with:
#   echo -n "your-passphrase" | shasum -a 256
# VITE_ADMIN_HASH=

# Web3Forms access key — powers the contact form on /connect.
# Get one free at https://web3forms.com (no account required, just an
# email to receive submissions at). It is inlined into the JS bundle at
# *build time* (see the note at the top of this file), so it ships in
# plain text to every visitor's browser — this is expected and safe:
# Web3Forms access keys are designed to be public, client-side values,
# not secrets. When this is unset, the contact form falls back to a
# `mailto:` link instead of submitting.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=

# --- Reverse-proxy hints (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Only needed if your shared Caddy stack inspects container env (e.g. a
# Caddy/nginx-proxy companion). Hard-coded label-based routes don't need these.
# VIRTUAL_HOST=avendavi.com
# LETSENCRYPT_HOST=avendavi.com
# LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=patriktjaderqvist@gmail.com
